Z||000000||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||12:15 AM||||Does anyone know much about this kit? I mean it look s great probably the best looking kit for the Fiero. Mainly because it doesn't make the car something it's not (like a Ferrari or Lambo). And well I know archie says it is easy to build is it? And the build quality? (no offence Archie).||||reg||1
Z||000001||rmorgandotcom||12-03-2001||12:32 AM||||How hard?, depends on your skill level.  Most stuff goes on fairly easy but there are some difficult things.(headlights)||||reg||1
Z||000002||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||12:40 AM||||I wouldn't argue that some things would be hard but I have heard about some be shipped out with let's say lesss the immaculate condition , and it requires quite the body man to make the kit look decent( no offence to anyone) <P>I just need to know if the car will need alot of fiberglass resign patches and stuff. I not really worried about putting the pieces of the puzzle together its kind of the pieces that worry me.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||12-03-2001||12:49 AM||||I've seen the raw panels for the Finale at Archie's place. The molds are very good. I would say once it's all together you would just need to do finishing work on them. There were very few if any pits or cracks. As with any kit the finish of the car is what you make it and the care used when assembling also is a big factor. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||01:09 AM||||Thanks phweh! At least I know that it won't be a horror story like some of those ferrari and diablo kits!!!||||reg||1
